      "statusChangeNewStatus": "closed",
      "value": "The \"Use Impostor\" option does not control whether or not you see impostors, it controls whether or not other people see your impostor.\n\nThese are the conditions under which you may see someone's impostor, with as much detail as I can provide:\n\n- The user you are observing has \"Use impostor as fallback\" enabled\n\nAND\n\n- The avatar they are wearing has had an impostor generated\n\nAND\n\n- If the impostor was generated recently, you've refreshed the avatar's information and see the latest version (this can be done by the wearer of the avatar switching away and back to the avatar)\n\nAND\n\n- You are not blocking the user or their avatar for safety reasons\n\nThen:\n\n- You have set your download size limit to lower than the avatar's download size\n\nOR\n\n- You are on a platform which does not have a version of that user's avatar (such as when you are on quest and they have a pc-only avatar)\n\nOR\n\n- You have set your avatar performance limit to lower than the avatar's performance rank UNLESS the avatar can be \"performance filtered\" down to a better performance by removing things like particle systems\n\nAs you can see, a lot of these are dependent on your own personal settings. It is very likely that you simply had different performance settings than your friend, and were not meeting these conditions. If you were, and it still does not load, please make a more detailed post about exactly which conditions you were attempting to fulfill.",
